* workflow: should the `/`-delimited target address go beyond `wf best status`?
  * `status` special-cases it: an address is a prefix of the `.wf/best` tree
    (`s2`, `s2/m4`, `s2/m4/g4`) meaning "every target under it". The prefix
    semantics are the point, and they are what justifies the form there.
  * every other `best` command acts on exactly one fully-qualified target and
    names it with `-g`/`-m` (`wf best gen s2 -g 4 dfs.seed`), which is already
    unambiguous. They would gain the syntax without the semantics.
  * so this is a consistency question, not a usability one: is one command
    taking a path while the rest take flags worth unifying?
  * `wf show` walks space-separated static layout parts consumed by
    layout_args, which is a different kind of argument; probably leave it.
  * see ../nutrimatic/plans/integrate-best-pairs.md for the design.

